---
import { contactEmail } from '../site';
const qs: [string, string][] = [
  ['Do I need to know anything about AI?', "No. You talk to him the way you'd talk to a person. If he doesn't understand, he says so and asks one question."],
  ['Can I set him up for my mum or dad?', 'Yes, that is who he is for. Setup walks through each permission the Mac asks for, with one button each, and takes a few minutes.'],
  ['What goes to the internet?', "Dictation, his memory and the reminders he says out loud stay on your Mac. When he has to think something through, he sends that one question, with the bits of memory it needs, to an online model. Your recordings never leave the Mac: he hears you and speaks on it. A to-do you ask for goes into Apple Reminders, and from there to your other Apple devices if you use iCloud."],
  ['Can he break something?', "He stops before anything that can't be undone, keeps copies of what he changes so \"undo that\" works, and stops the moment you press esc. Passwords, card numbers and security settings he never touches."],
  ['Does he work without the internet?', "Dictation does, and so does his voice. Reminders he has already set he says at the right time without going online. Questions he has to think about, and work he does for you, need a connection."],
  ['Can he write an email for me?', "Yes. Click into the reply, hold the talk key and say what you want to answer. He reads the email on your screen, writes the answer and puts it right into the field. Nothing is sent: you read it and press Send. \"Undo that\" takes it out again."],
  ['Is he fast?', "Dictation lands about half a second after you let go of the key, because it's done on your Mac. His voice is made on your Mac too, so he starts speaking as soon as he knows his first sentence. A spoken answer usually starts in about two seconds."],
  ['Will he be in the way?', "No. When nothing is going on, he flies off the screen after 15 seconds, and swoops back the moment you hold a key to talk or dictate. He stays while a question or a card is waiting for you. In Settings he can stay longer, or for good."],
  ['Which Macs does he run on?', 'Macs with Apple silicon, so M1 or newer, with macOS 14 Sonoma or later. Only Macs for now.'],
  ['Which languages does he speak?', 'He answers in the language you speak to him in. English and German are the ones we test most, and the two his voice speaks.'],
  ['Why a bird?', "Wrens are small, loud for their size, and nest in the corners of houses. That's where Milo lives too."],
  ['When can I get him?', "He's being tested now. Join the waitlist and we'll write to you once, when he's ready, and not before."],
];
---
<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap faq-grid">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions people ask.</h2>
      <p>Something missing? <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>Write to us</a>, a person answers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      {qs.map(([q, a]) => (
        <details>
          <summary><span>{q}</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
          <p>{a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-grid { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) { .faq-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); align-items: start; } .faq-grid .section-head { position: sticky; top: 7rem; } }
  .faq { border-top: 1.5px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  summary {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 0.2rem;
    font-weight: 650; font-size: 1.12rem;
    cursor: pointer; list-style: none;
    border-radius: 0.4rem;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary:hover span { color: var(--lavender-deep); }
  summary i { position: relative; flex: none; width: 1.6rem; height: 1.6rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--lavender-wash); transition: transform 300ms var(--ease-spring), background-color 200ms; }
  summary i::before, summary i::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; width: 0.7rem; height: 2px; margin: -1px 0 0 -0.35rem; border-radius: 1px; background: var(--lavender-deep); }
  summary i::after { transform: rotate(90deg); transition: transform 300ms var(--ease-spring); }
  details[open] summary i { background: var(--lavender); transform: rotate(180deg); }
  details[open] summary i::before, details[open] summary i::after { background: var(--on-lavender); }
  details[open] summary i::after { transform: rotate(0deg); }
  details p { padding: 0 2.6rem 1.3rem 0.2rem; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 40rem; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    details::details-content { block-size: 0; overflow: clip; transition: block-size 320ms var(--ease-out), content-visibility 320ms allow-discrete; }
    details[open]::details-content { block-size: auto; }
    :root { interpolate-size: allow-keywords; }
  }
</style>
